image,menu_zm_weapons_mc96
material,menu_zm_weapons_mc96
camo,camo_mc96
// ============================================================================
//  THESE FOUR ARE OWNED ON PURPOSE. DO NOT UN-OWN THEM. Attempted twice now,
//  crashed once, blocked by measurement the second time (2026-08-29, 2026-08-30).
//
//  ---- WHY THEY LOOK REMOVABLE ------------------------------------------------
//  ROOT CAUSE OF THE SILENT M1911 (user report, 2026-08-29). The donor mod.ff
//  these were inherited from renamed their fire-sound aliases:
//
//      donor / this mod            retail BO2
//      wpn_m1911_fire_plr    ->    wpn_1911_fire_plr      (no 'm')
//      wpn_m1911_fire_npc    ->    wpn_1911_fire_npc
//      wpn_m1911_*_pap       ->    wpn_1911_*_pap
//      wpn_m1911_dryfire_*   ->    wpn_1911_dryfire_*
//      wpn_mc96_fire_plr     ->    wpn_1911_fire_plr      (the C96 shares them)
//
//  Those wpn_m1911_* / wpn_mc96_* names exist ONLY in the donor's alias table.
//  The user's optional sound pack in storage\t6\zone replaces the payload behind
//  RETAIL's wpn_1911_*, which this mod's weapon then never asks for - so their
//  custom M1911 is unreachable, and since v2.7.3 trimmed mod.all to additions
//  only, the name resolves nowhere and the gun is fully silent. Same for the C96.
//  The tempting fix is therefore "stop declaring them, let retail supply them".
//
//  ---- WHY THAT IS WRONG, MEASURED 2026-08-30 --------------------------------
//  mod.ff LOADS BEFORE EVERY MAP. Owning these is what makes them exist on maps
//  whose own fastfile has never carried them. Unlinker --list over the retail
//  fastfiles in H:\Backups\Game Files\pluto_t6_full_game\zone\all:
//
//      m1911_zm, m1911_upgraded_zm, m1911lh_upgraded_zm
//                     -> zm_nuked, zm_prison, zm_buried, zm_transit, zm_highrise
//                        ... but NOT zm_tomb
//      c96_zm, c96_upgraded_zm
//                     -> zm_tomb ONLY
//
//  And this mod hands both out cross-map, unconditionally:
//      quality_of_life.gsc:658   precacheitem( "c96_zm" )     <- root, EVERY map
//      quality_of_life.gsc:695   precacheitem( "m1911_zm" )   <- incl. Origins
//      zm_nuked.gsc:738  zm_buried.gsc:135  zm_highrise.gsc:569
//      zm_prison.gsc:151         include_weapon( "c96_zm" ) + add_zombie_weapon
//
//  So un-owning c96_zm removes the C96 from Nuketown, Buried, Die Rise and Mob,
//  and un-owning m1911_zm removes the M1911 from Origins. That is a feature loss
//  on five maps, not a sound tweak.
//
//  ---- THE 2026-08-29 12:00 CRASH, RE-DIAGNOSED ------------------------------
//  The first attempt dropped the four weapon lines and the game took an access
//  violation (0xC0000005) part way through loading NUKETOWN, right after
//  `CSC Executed "scripts/zm/zm_nuked/zm_nuked::main()"`. It was recorded at the
//  time as a dangling camo->weapon pointer. THAT DIAGNOSIS IS WRONG: a dumped
//  weaponCamo has NO weapon field at all - only baseMaterial / camoMaterial /
//  patternCamoImage / solidCamoImage. The reference runs the OTHER way; the
//  weapon file ends with `\camo\camo_mc96`.
//  🌟 The mechanism that actually fits: zm_nuked.gsc:738 is include_weapon(
//  "c96_zm" ), retail Nuketown has no c96_zm, and the crash lands on that map
//  immediately after that script runs.
//
//  ---- WHAT A REAL FIX WOULD HAVE TO DO --------------------------------------
//  Keep supplying these five assets on the maps retail lacks them, while making
//  the guns ask for retail's alias spellings. A raw weapons\zm\ file CANNOT do
//  it: the Linker is FIRST-LOAD-WINS, zone_source\base\mod.ff is the first
//  --load, and a corrected raw file was written and relinked and the rebuilt
//  asset STILL carried wpn_m1911_*. Linker.exe has no override flag. That leaves
//  (a) linking an intermediate fastfile from corrected raw sources and --loading
//  it BEFORE the donor, or (b) accepting mod.all-supplied wpn_m1911_* rows, which
//  makes the guns audible in the MOD's flavour rather than the user's. Neither is
//  a one-line change; both need the user's call.
//
//  📝 Verified along the way: retail's own camo_m1911 carries the SAME 22 camo
//  entries as the donor's, differing only in material coverage (1 base / 2 camo
//  vs 5 / 6), so the animated camo was never the real stake here.
// ============================================================================
